 "title": "Coupled sagittal and lateral moments during axial rotation at 30-100% MVC, standing, chronic LBP patients (normalised)",
 "subcategory": "coupled moments in axial rotation",
 "quantity": {
  "name": "coupled moment",
  "definition": "mean coupled torque in sagittal/coronal planes during R/L axial rotation, normalised to the subject's maximal torque in that direction (from the 6 MVCs); + flexion, + right lateral flexion",
  "unit": "% of MVC moment in that direction"
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Erect standing in a B200 Isostation triaxial dynamometer locked in 3 planes, L5-S1 interspinous space aligned with its flexion/extension axis; pelvis and lower legs stabilised (pelvic restraint, thigh and knee straps); torso fixed by chest restraint and thoracic pad; arms folded across chest. MVCs (5 s, randomised, 2 min rest) in flexion, extension, R/L lateral flexion, R/L axial rotation with visual feedback and verbal encouragement; then R/L axial rotation at 70, 50, 30% MVC to a visual target. Mean of stable 3 s; baseline (relaxed standing in device) subtracted. Same lab/protocol as Ng 2001.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Upright standing, pelvis fixed, thorax restrained",
   "Axial rotation at 30/50/70/100% of axial MVC (controls ≈ 84 Nm)",
   "Report coupled flexion/extension and lateral moments at L5-S1, normalised by the model's MVC in those directions (controls: flexion 125, extension 180, lateral 138/147 Nm in Fig 1)"
  ],
  "subject_model": {
   "sex": "M",
   "age": 28.3,
   "height_cm": 177,
   "weight_kg": 72.1,
   "disc_area_mm2": null,
   "source": "Table 1 (back pain patients)"
  },
  "notes": "Can be converted to Nm only approximately using group-mean MVCs (Fig 1); not done here. Trend (P=0.08) for larger coupled flexion in patients during left rotation."
 },
